        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: десятилетие",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "десятилетие (desyatilétiye) — \"a decade\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "За последнее десятилетие город сильно изменился. Za poslédneye desyatilétiye górod sílno izmenílsya. Over the last decade the town has changed a lot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. Ten years: десять лет."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "десятилетие (desyatilétiye) joins десять \"ten\" and лето \"summer\", which is inherited from Proto-Slavic lěto \"year\" (EtymDB): ten years."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
